WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Before the play has even started,
one figure steps forward,

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.790
holding a scroll.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:11.660
In 14 lines, he tells us everything:
"Doth with their death bury their parents’

4
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:12.960
strife."

5
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:18.150
Then the play begins: a street fight, and
soon two young people meet at a party,

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.230
smiling.

7
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.240
A clock starts to tick.

8
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.280
The ending is out before the story starts.

9
00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.740
So why would Shakespeare give
it away in the first minute?

10
00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.130
In this mission, you'll take
the Prologue apart as a sonnet,

11
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.680
rhyme by rhyme.

12
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.450
You'll map the story act by
act, up to its turning point.

13
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.750
And you'll weigh the big question
running through the play:

14
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.760
is it fate, or the choices people make?

15
00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.940
Your mission: explain why
Shakespeare gives the ending away.
